===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q503}} An elongated curved tropical fruit of a {{vern|banana plant}}, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. {{defdate|from 1597}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2017|author={{w|Sam Shepard}}|title=Spy of the First Person|chapter=27|url=|page=62|text=I'll need a few things. I'll need some mayonnaise and a silver tin of sardines, a '''banana'''. |isbn=9780525521563}}
## {{lb|en|North America|UK|Ireland}} In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana [[cultivar]], which may be eaten raw, as distinct from e.g. a [[plantain]] for cooking.
# The tropical tree-like plant which bears clusters of bananas, a plant of the genus ''[[Musa]]'' (but sometimes also including plants from {{taxfmt|Ensete|genus}}), which has large, elongated leaves. {{defdate|from 1697}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A yellow color, like that of a banana's skin. {{defdate|from 1923}}
#: {{color panel|FFE135}}
# {{lb|en|pejorative|ethnic slur}} A person of [[East Asian|East]] or [[Southeast Asian]] [[descent]], [[consider]]ed to be [[overly]] [[assimilated]] and [[subservient]] to [[white]] [[authority]]. {{defdate|from 1970}}
#: {{syn|en|Twinkie}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} The [[penis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=_6cgAQAAMAAJ|title=Cop Feels of Three Men's "Privates"|author=Christopher Street|volume=10|text=The fact that the cop bought O'Brien a beer after feeling of his '''banana''' suggests that it must have been a promising one}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Sarah Miynowski|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=lg0mATRb6EAC&pg=PT36|title=Fishbowl|page=36|text=His you-know-what turned soft .. his eight o'clock class was the last thing on his mind five minutes ago, when his '''banana''' wasn't overripe.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Anthony Bunko|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=MdBxBAAAQBAJ&pg=PT71|title=Lord Forgive Me|page=71|text=Most of the gang were trying their best to shag the girls. One boy was sitting in a tree playing with himself and another was asking a table of teenagers if they would like to see his '''banana'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=4pQ4DwAAQBAJ&pg=PA234|title=Intimate Relationships in Cinema, Literature and Visual Culture|page=234|text=He adds that after eating his '''banana''' (sucking his penis), he wants anal sex, but she asks him to lick her pussy. Then he tells her no because it is disgusting.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[banana kick]].
# {{lb|en|nuclear physics}} A [[banana equivalent dose]].
# {{lb|en|computer science|colloquial}} A [[catamorphism]] (from the use of [[banana bracket]]s in the notation).

